{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27268624","formula":"C₁₄H₁₈N₂","hill":"C14H18N2","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":18.0,"N":2.0},"names":{"en":"3-(1-methylpiperidin-4-yl)-1H-indole"},"descriptions":{"en":"SN-22, also known as 3-(1-methyl-4-piperidinyl)indole, is a serotonin receptor modulator of the piperidinylindole group related to the psychedelic drug dimethyltryptamine (DMT). Though it is not technically a tryptamine itself, SN-22 can be regarded as a constrained analogue of DMT. The drug shows affinity for the serotonin 5-HT1A and 5-HT2A receptors (Ki = 146–514 nM and 19–67 nM, respectively). A deuterated isotopologue of SN-22 is known to be a serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonist, albeit with lower potency than DMT. The chemical synthesis of SN-22 has been described."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":11206672,"mass":214.31,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1CCC(CC1)C2=CNC3=CC=CC=C32","inchikey":"KYSCKYJNMTUJPA-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-(1-methylpiperidin-4-yl)-1H-indole","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11206672","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.971,"y":0.016,"z":-0.001,"el":"N"},{"x":1.969,"y":1.998,"z":-0.001,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.041,"y":-0.12,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.85,"y":0.232,"z":-1.258,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.851,"y":0.234,"z":1.258,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.247,"y":-0.392,"z":-1.212,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.248,"y":-0.39,"z":1.212,"el":"C"},{"x":0.338,"y":0.5,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":1.575,"y":-0.198,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.609,"y":1.846,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.323,"y":-0.542,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":2.585,"y":0.766,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":1.937,"y":-1.56,"z":0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":3.945,"y":0.436,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":3.294,"y":-1.905,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":4.28,"y":-0.921,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.916,"y":-1.212,"z":0.002,"el":"H"},{"x